        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "bcc2014d-870b-5a09-84a0-64af56c1a11a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Liaoyang, Changchun, Liaoning province, Jilin province, T'ai-tzu River, People's Republic of China\n- People: Yuan Baojing\n- Organizations: Northeast Normal University\n- Concepts: 2010 census of China, metro area, national normal universities\n\nFacts:\n- Yuan Baojing was born on 16 February 1966 and was a Chinese billionaire from Liaoyang in Liaoning province.\n- In 2010, Liaoyang was a prefecture-level city in east-central Liaoning province in the People's Republic of China, situated on the T'ai-tzu River.\n- In 2010, Liaoyang and Anshan together formed a metro area with 2,057,200 inhabitants.\n- According to the 2010 census of China, Changchun had a total population of 7,674,439 under its jurisdiction.\n- Northeast Normal University, often abbreviated NENU or 东北师大, is located in Changchun in Jilin province.\n- Northeast Normal University is one of the six national normal universities in the People's Republic of China.\n- Yuan Baojing died on 17 March 2006.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
